This image, corresponding to Fig. 2(A) and (B) in the PDF, illustrates the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image (left) reveals spherical, dendrimer-like a-D-glucan nanoparticles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, generally appearing as single particles or occasional pairs. The Dynamic Light Scattering (DLS) data (right) quantifies the size distribution, showing a uniform population with an average hydrodynamic diameter concentrated around 70-80 nm, consistent with the text's description of their nanoscale properties.